msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContributionKind|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Contribution Kind"
msgstr "贡献种类"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContributionKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Whether a recorded contribution came from a model, a human operator, or a tool. Closed and mandatory on every contribution, because the three carry different authority: a model contribution is advice, an operator contribution may be a decision, and a tool contribution is an observation. A review surface that cannot distinguish them cannot tell a reader who actually decided."
msgstr "所记录的贡献究竟出自模型、人类操作者，抑或工具。此项封闭且对每一条贡献均为必备，因为三者所具权威各不相同：模型贡献是建议，操作者贡献可以是决定，工具贡献则是观察。无从分辨三者的复核界面，也就无法告诉读者究竟是谁作的决定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContributionKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:draftComment gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionModel ."
msgstr "示例：ex:draftComment gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionModel ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EnactmentIsNotOccurrenceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "an enactment is generated by an occurrence, never identical to one"
msgstr "实施由某次occurrence生成，绝不等同于它"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EnactmentIsNotOccurrenceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:Constraint rejecting a logic:Enactment typed as a calendar event. The schedule is the GENERATOR and the enactment is generated: identifying them makes a skipped occurrence indistinguishable from a missing run, and makes an enactment that outlives its scheduled slot unrepresentable."
msgstr "拒斥被类型化为日历事件之 logic:Enactment 的 logic:Constraint。日程是生成者，实施是被生成者：将二者等同，会使「被跳过的 occurrence」与「缺失的运行」无从分辨，也使「超出既定时段仍在进行的实施」无从表达。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ExplanationCarriesProofConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "an explanation carries a checkable proof"
msgstr "解释须载可核验之证明"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ExplanationCarriesProofConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:Constraint rejecting a gmeow:FrontierExplanation that carries no proof. An explanation whose supporting derivation is absent is a narrative, and a narrative presented where a proof belongs is exactly the substitution the advice-is-never-authority discipline forbids."
msgstr "拒斥不载证明之 gmeow:FrontierExplanation 的 logic:Constraint。缺失佐证推导的解释只是一段叙述；而在本应是证明之处呈上叙述，正是「建议绝非权威」这一纪律所禁止的偷换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FrontierExplanation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Frontier Explanation"
msgstr "前沿解释"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FrontierExplanation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Why one frontier entry carries the position it does, in the five terms an operator actually needs: the proof, the evidence, the governing policy, the cost/risk/benefit criteria, and the DISSENTING attributed observations. Dissent is a required content rather than a courtesy — an explanation that presents only the supporting view has told the operator what to think rather than what is known."
msgstr "某个前沿条目何以居于其位，用操作者真正需要的五项来说明：证明、证据、治理策略、成本/风险/收益准则，以及持异议的具名观察。异议属必备内容而非礼节性附带——只呈现支持性观点的解释，等于告诉操作者该怎么想，而不是告诉他已知的是什么。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FrontierExplanation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:ocrWhyBlocked a gmeow:FrontierExplanation ; gmeow:explanationDissent ex:reviewerObjection ."
msgstr "示例：ex:ocrWhyBlocked a gmeow:FrontierExplanation ; gmeow:explanationDissent ex:reviewerObjection ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GuidanceSet|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Guidance Set"
msgstr "指导集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GuidanceSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The versioned body of rubrics and checklists governing how a cluster's work is done. Versioned through the standard version-membership relator rather than a bespoke mechanism, because 'which guidance governed THAT occurrence' must stay answerable after the guidance has moved on — and an unversioned guidance set silently rewrites the past every time it is edited."
msgstr "统辖某簇工作如何开展的、经版本化的评量表与清单集合。它通过标准的版本归属关系来版本化，而非另设机制，因为「当初那一次 occurrence 受哪一版指导统辖」必须在指导演进之后仍然可答——而未版本化的指导集，每被编辑一次，就悄然改写一次过去。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GuidanceSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adrGuidanceV2 a gmeow:GuidanceSet ; gmeow:guidanceRubric ex:adrRubric ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adrGuidanceV2 a gmeow:GuidanceSet ; gmeow:guidanceRubric ex:adrRubric ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GuidanceVersionRecordedConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "an occurrence records the guidance version that governed it"
msgstr "occurrence须记录governing之指导版本"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GuidanceVersionRecordedConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:Constraint rejecting a logic:ContextAssembly that names no governing guidance version. Without it, 'was that occurrence done right?' can only be judged against today's guidance, which silently rewrites the past every time the guidance is edited."
msgstr "拒斥未指明任何 governing 指导版本之 logic:ContextAssembly 的 logic:Constraint。缺了它，「那次 occurrence 做得对不对」就只能拿今天的指导去衡量，于是每编辑一次指导，就悄然改写一次过去。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ReviewProjectionCompletenessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "a review projection carries all eight contents and a receipt"
msgstr "复核投影须载全部八项内容及一份回执"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ReviewProjectionCompletenessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:Constraint rejecting a gmeow:WorkReviewProjection missing any of its eight contents or its projection receipt. Partial completeness is the failure mode that matters here: an operator view that silently omits effect status or dissent looks complete and is not, and the receipt is what discloses the collapse the view necessarily performs."
msgstr "拒斥「缺其八项内容之一、或缺其投影回执」之 gmeow:WorkReviewProjection 的 logic:Constraint。此处真正要紧的失效样态是「部分完整」：一个悄然略去效应状态或异议的操作者视图，看上去完整而实则不然；而回执正是用来披露该视图必然施加之塌缩的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/WorkCluster|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Work Cluster"
msgstr "工作簇"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/WorkCluster|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A CONTINUING body of work: a standing goal, the policy governing it, the recurrence that issues occurrences, the prescription version currently in force, the guidance that governs how it is done, and the working memory it has accumulated. It is the thing that persists between occurrences and is never itself enacted — enactments are what its recurrence generates. Typed APART from logic:Enactment, which is one occurrence, and from logic:Plan, which is the prescription: a cluster OWNS a prescription and outlives every version of it."
msgstr "一项持续进行的工作体：一个长期目标、统辖它的策略、发出各次 occurrence 的周期性、当前生效的规定版本、统辖其做法的指导，以及它所累积的工作记忆。它是在各次 occurrence 之间存续之物，其自身从不被实施——实施乃是其周期性所生成者。它与 logic:Enactment（单次 occurrence）及 logic:Plan（规定）分开类型化：一个簇拥有一份规定，并且比该规定的每一个版本都活得更久。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/WorkCluster|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adrReview a gmeow:WorkCluster ; gmeow:clusterSchedule ex:weeklySchedule ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adrReview a gmeow:WorkCluster ; gmeow:clusterSchedule ex:weeklySchedule ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/WorkReviewProjection|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Work Review Projection"
msgstr "工作复核投影"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/WorkReviewProjection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The comprehensive operator view of a cluster, carrying all eight required contents: the continuing goal and its recurrence, the current prescription and its revision lineage, the current occurrence and its exact input generation, the derived frontier with recommendations and blockers, approvals and pending inputs, effect and reconciliation and compensation status, accumulated notes and decisions and artifacts and receipts and prior-occurrence comparison, and an exact accessible graph or timeline representation. It is a PROJECTION and says so: it necessarily collapses standpoint-indexed classifications into one readable surface, and that loss is disclosed on its receipt rather than hidden."
msgstr "对某个簇的完备操作者视图，载有全部八项必备内容：持续目标及其周期性；当前规定及其修订沿革；当前 occurrence 及其所固定的确切输入世代；带推荐与阻塞的导出前沿；审批与待办输入；效应、核实与补偿的状态；累积的备注、决定、产出物、回执以及与既往 occurrence 的比对；还有一份精确且无障碍的图或时间线呈现。它是一项投影，并且明说这一点：它必然把按立场索引的各种分类塌缩为单一可读界面，而该项损失记在它的回执上，而非被掩盖。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/WorkReviewProjection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:w12Review a gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ; gmeow:reviewReceipt ex:w12Receipt ."
msgstr "示例：ex:w12Review a gmeow:WorkReviewProjection ; gmeow:reviewReceipt ex:w12Receipt ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/approvalGoverningNorm|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "approval governing norm"
msgstr "治理审批之规范"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/approvalGoverningNorm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The domain binding of the kernel's approval-policy seam onto the norms spine. Specializes the kernel property, so a commitment's policy is a real norm rather than an opaque reference."
msgstr "把内核的「审批—策略」接缝绑定到规范骨架上的领域绑定。它特化内核属性，使一项承诺所依的策略是一条真实的规范，而非一个不透明的引用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/approvalGoverningNorm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:publishApproval gmeow:approvalGoverningNorm ex:publicationPolicy ."
msgstr "示例：ex:publishApproval gmeow:approvalGoverningNorm ex:publicationPolicy ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterActivePrescription|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "cluster active prescription"
msgstr "簇之现行规定"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterActivePrescription|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The prescription version new occurrences will be enacted against. Functional, and deliberately a POINTER: an enactment pins its version at start, so moving this pointer mid-flight revises what happens next without rewriting what is already running."
msgstr "新的各次 occurrence 将据以实施的规定版本。此属性为函数性的，且刻意设为一个指针：实施在开始时便固定其版本，因此中途移动该指针只改变此后发生之事，而不改写已在运行之事。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterActivePrescription|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterActivePrescription ex:reviewProcessV4 ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterActivePrescription ex:reviewProcessV4 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterEnactment|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "cluster enactment"
msgstr "簇之实施"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterEnactment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "One occurrence the cluster has generated. Multi-valued and append-only: this is the cluster's history, and a prior occurrence stays readable and comparable after later ones begin."
msgstr "该簇已生成的一次 occurrence。多值且只增不改：这就是簇的历史，先前的 occurrence 在后续者开始之后依然可读、可比对。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterEnactment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterEnactment ex:weekTwelve , ex:weekThirteen ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterEnactment ex:weekTwelve , ex:weekThirteen ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterGoal|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "cluster goal"
msgstr "簇之目标"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The continuing goal the cluster exists to serve. Where that goal is a maintenance goal, a successful occurrence never closes it — the goal is satisfied only while its condition holds, so the cluster keeps recurring by design rather than by oversight."
msgstr "该簇存在所要服务的持续目标。若该目标属维持性目标，则一次成功的 occurrence 绝不会将其了结——目标仅在其条件成立期间被满足，故该簇之所以不断重复，是出于设计而非疏忽。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterGoal ex:decisionsStayReviewed ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterGoal ex:decisionsStayReviewed ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterGuidanceSet|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "cluster guidance set"
msgstr "簇之指导集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterGuidanceSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The guidance currently governing the cluster. Functional, and a pointer like the active prescription: an occurrence records the version it actually ran under rather than inheriting whatever this later points at."
msgstr "当前统辖该簇的指导。此属性为函数性的，且与现行规定一样是个指针：一次 occurrence 记录它实际据以运行的那一版，而非承继此指针日后所指之物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterGuidanceSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterGuidanceSet ex:reviewGuidance ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterGuidanceSet ex:reviewGuidance ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterNote|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "cluster note"
msgstr "簇之备注"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterNote|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A retained note the cluster carries between occurrences — its working memory. Multi-valued. Retention is the point: a cluster that forgets what the last occurrence learned is a schedule, not a continuing body of work."
msgstr "该簇在各次 occurrence 之间携带的留存备注——即其工作记忆。多值。留存正是关键所在：一个把上次 occurrence 所学尽数遗忘的簇，只是一份日程表，而非一项持续进行的工作体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterNote|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterNote ex:deprecationBacklogNote ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterNote ex:deprecationBacklogNote ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterOccurrenceSeries|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "cluster occurrence series"
msgstr "簇之occurrence序列"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterOccurrenceSeries|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The series of concrete occurrences the cluster's schedule has issued, reached through the events spine. Reused, never re-minted: the recurrence rule belongs to the series and a skipped occurrence is a schedule exception rather than a missing member."
msgstr "该簇的日程所发出的一系列具体 occurrence，经由事件骨架抵达。此处是复用而非重铸：周期规则属于该序列，而被跳过的一次 occurrence 是一项日程例外，并非一个缺失的成员。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterOccurrenceSeries|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterOccurrenceSeries ex:weeklyReviewSeries ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterOccurrenceSeries ex:weeklyReviewSeries ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "cluster policy"
msgstr "簇之策略"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The norm governing how the cluster's work may be carried out — what requires approval, what is forbidden, who may decide. Non-functional: several norms may govern one cluster, and where they disagree the disagreement is data rather than an error to resolve by picking one."
msgstr "统辖该簇之工作可以如何开展的规范——何者需经审批、何者被禁止、谁有权决定。非函数性：可有数条规范同时统辖一个簇；它们相左之处，其分歧本身即是数据，而非一个「随便择一」便可了结的错误。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterPolicy ex:reviewPolicy ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterPolicy ex:reviewPolicy ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterSchedule|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "cluster schedule"
msgstr "簇之日程"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterSchedule|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The schedule that issues the cluster's occurrences, mediating the recurrence rule and the generated events. Reuses the calendar spine rather than minting a recurrence vocabulary: the schedule is the GENERATOR, and an enactment is generated by an occurrence rather than being one."
msgstr "发出该簇各次 occurrence 的日程，居中联结周期规则与所生成的事件。此处复用日历骨架，而非另铸一套周期词汇：日程是生成者，而实施乃由 occurrence 所生成，并非其本身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterSchedule|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterSchedule ex:weeklyThursday ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adrReviewCluster gmeow:clusterSchedule ex:weeklyThursday ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionKind|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "contribution kind"
msgstr "贡献种类"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a recorded contribution to its exactly-one kind. Domain a contribution record (stated in prose). Functional and mandatory."
msgstr "把一条已记录的贡献关联到它唯一的那种类别。定义域为一条贡献记录（以散文陈述）。函数性且为必备。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:draftSummary gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionModel ."
msgstr "示例：ex:draftSummary gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionModel ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionModel|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "model contribution"
msgstr "模型贡献"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Generated by a model. Always advice: it may inform a decision and may never be one, and it may never authorize an effect."
msgstr "由模型生成。它永远只是建议：可以为决定提供参考，却绝不能成为决定，也绝不能授权任何效应。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionOperator|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "operator contribution"
msgstr "操作者贡献"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Made by a human operator. The only kind that may carry a decision, and the kind an approval commitment names."
msgstr "由人类操作者作出。这是唯一可以承载决定的类别，也是审批承诺所指名的那一类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionTool|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "tool contribution"
msgstr "工具贡献"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionTool|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Produced by a deterministic tool. An observation rather than advice or decision: it reports what a tool found, and its authority is the tool's correctness."
msgstr "由确定性工具产出。它是观察，而非建议或决定：它报告某工具之所见，其权威即该工具的正确性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/criterionMagnitude|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "criterion magnitude"
msgstr "准则量值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/criterionMagnitude|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The dimensioned magnitude a cost, risk, benefit, budget or deadline criterion carries, grounded in the math: quantity spine so it travels with its dimension rather than as a bare number. Domain a criterion or budget record (stated in prose). A quantitative claim with no dimension is an ungrounded number."
msgstr "成本、风险、收益、预算或期限一类准则所携带的带量纲量值，锚定于 math: 的量骨架，从而随其量纲一同流转，而非以裸数字的形式漂移。定义域为一条准则或预算记录（以散文陈述）。无量纲的定量主张，只是一个未经锚定的数字。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/criterionMagnitude|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:timeToRestore gmeow:criterionMagnitude ex:ninetySeconds ."
msgstr "示例：ex:timeToRestore gmeow:criterionMagnitude ex:ninetySeconds ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/enactmentContextAssembly|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "enactment context assembly"
msgstr "实施之上下文汇集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/enactmentContextAssembly|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The record of what was surfaced to this occurrence and what was withheld — the binding that makes 'which notes were surfaced to this run, under which guidance version' answerable. Functional: one assembly per occurrence, so the answer is unambiguous."
msgstr "记录本次 occurrence 究竟被呈上了什么、又被扣下了什么——正是这项绑定使「这一次运行被呈上了哪些备注、依的又是哪一版指导」成为可答之问。函数性：每次 occurrence 恰有一份汇集，答案因而没有歧义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/enactmentContextAssembly|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:weekThirteen gmeow:enactmentContextAssembly ex:week13Context ."
msgstr "示例：ex:weekThirteen gmeow:enactmentContextAssembly ex:week13Context ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/entryHardFailure|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "entry hard failure"
msgstr "条目硬失败"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/entryHardFailure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The verifier verdict blocking a frontier entry, reusing preference's hard/soft constraint apparatus. A hard failure may not be traded away by a favourable score elsewhere, which is exactly the guarantee the reused vocabulary already enforces."
msgstr "阻塞某个前沿条目的校验裁断，复用偏好切片的硬/软约束装置。硬失败不得以别处的有利评分来抵换——而这正是所复用的那套词汇本已施行的保证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/entryHardFailure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:ocrEntry gmeow:entryHardFailure ex:capabilityVerdict ."
msgstr "示例：ex:ocrEntry gmeow:entryHardFailure ex:capabilityVerdict ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explainsEntry|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "explains entry"
msgstr "解释某条目"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explainsEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an explanation to the frontier entry it accounts for. Functional."
msgstr "把一项解释关联到它所交代的那个前沿条目。函数性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explainsEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explainsEntry ex:rollbackEntry ."
msgstr "示例：ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explainsEntry ex:rollbackEntry ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationCriterion|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "explanation criterion"
msgstr "解释之准则"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationCriterion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A cost, risk or benefit criterion bearing on the entry, reusing the norms criterion vocabulary. Its magnitudes ground in the math: quantity spine rather than travelling as bare numbers. Multi-valued."
msgstr "作用于该条目的一项成本、风险或收益准则，复用规范切片的准则词汇。其量值锚定于 math: 的量骨架，而非以裸数字流转。多值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationCriterion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationCriterion ex:timeToRestore ."
msgstr "示例：ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationCriterion ex:timeToRestore ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationDissent|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "explanation dissent"
msgstr "解释所载异议"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationDissent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An attributed observation that DISAGREES with the entry's position. Range an attributed observation (stated in prose). Multi-valued and required where dissent exists: suppressing it turns coexisting standpoints into a manufactured consensus, which is the failure the whole preference apparatus exists to prevent."
msgstr "与该条目所处位置相左的一条具名观察。值域为一条具名观察（以散文陈述）。多值，且凡有异议之处即为必备：将其抹去，便把并存的诸立场变成了一份人造共识——而这正是整套偏好装置存在所要防止的失效。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationDissent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationDissent ex:onCallObjection ."
msgstr "示例：ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationDissent ex:onCallObjection ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationEvidence|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "explanation evidence"
msgstr "解释之证据"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationEvidence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Evidence bearing on the entry's position. Range an evidence node (stated in prose). Multi-valued."
msgstr "作用于该条目所处位置的证据。值域为一个证据节点（以散文陈述）。多值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationEvidence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationEvidence ex:incidentTimeline ."
msgstr "示例：ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationEvidence ex:incidentTimeline ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "explanation policy"
msgstr "解释所依策略"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The norm governing the entry's position. Multi-valued: where several norms bear on one action and disagree, all are surfaced."
msgstr "统辖该条目所处位置的规范。多值：当数条规范同时作用于一项行动且彼此相左时，全部予以呈现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationPolicy ex:fastestRestore ."
msgstr "示例：ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationPolicy ex:fastestRestore ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationProof|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "explanation proof"
msgstr "解释之证明项"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationProof|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The checkable derivation supporting the entry's position. Range a proof or derivation reference (stated in prose). A model-generated narrative may never occupy this position."
msgstr "支撑该条目所处位置的可核验推导。值域为一项证明或一个推导引用（以散文陈述）。由模型生成的叙述绝不可占据此位。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationProof|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationProof ex:proofTerm ."
msgstr "示例：ex:rollbackExplanation gmeow:explanationProof ex:proofTerm ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/frontierCandidateSet|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "frontier candidate set"
msgstr "前沿之候选集"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/frontierCandidateSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The frontier's candidate actions as a preference candidate set, so contextual comparison runs through the EXISTING preference apparatus instead of a second recommendation model. Functional. This is the binding that gives the frontier ties, incomparability and the no-global-winner discipline for free."
msgstr "把前沿的各候选行动作为一个偏好候选集，从而使语境化比较经由既有的偏好装置进行，而不是另起一套推荐模型。函数性。正是这项绑定，让前沿白得了并列、不可比，以及「无全局赢家」这一纪律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/frontierCandidateSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:remediationFrontier gmeow:frontierCandidateSet ex:remediationOptions ."
msgstr "示例：ex:remediationFrontier gmeow:frontierCandidateSet ex:remediationOptions ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/frontierComparisonContext|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "frontier comparison context"
msgstr "前沿之比较语境"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/frontierComparisonContext|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The context a frontier's recommendations are relative to. Functional. Recommendations without a context are the context-free global winner the preference apparatus exists to forbid, so this binding is what keeps a ranking honest."
msgstr "某前沿之推荐所相对的那个语境。函数性。没有语境的推荐，就是偏好装置存在所要禁止的那种「脱离语境的全局赢家」；因此正是这项绑定使排名保持诚实。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/frontierComparisonContext|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:remediationFrontier gmeow:frontierComparisonContext ex:fastestRestore ."
msgstr "示例：ex:remediationFrontier gmeow:frontierComparisonContext ex:fastestRestore ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceChecklist|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "guidance checklist"
msgstr "指导清单"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceChecklist|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A checklist the guidance set applies. Range an information object carrying the checklist content, whose textual surface grounds in the lang: form vocabulary. Multi-valued."
msgstr "该指导集所施用的一份清单。值域为承载清单内容的一个信息对象，其文本表层锚定于 lang: 的形式词汇。多值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceChecklist|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceChecklist ex:adrChecklist ."
msgstr "示例：ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceChecklist ex:adrChecklist ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceRendering|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "guidance rendering"
msgstr "指导之呈现"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceRendering|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The lang:-grounded textual surface of a guidance item, note, dissent or review rendering — the seam through which this slice's prose content gets a linguistic form rather than floating as an untyped literal. Range a lang: rendering (stated in prose). Domain any item carrying authored prose (stated in prose)."
msgstr "某项指导条目、备注、异议或复核呈现之文本表层，锚定于 lang:——正是这道接缝使本切片的散文内容获得语言学形式，而不至于以未类型化的字面量漂浮。值域为一个 lang: 呈现（以散文陈述）；定义域为任何承载撰写散文的条目（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceRendering|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceRendering ex:checklistMarkdown ."
msgstr "示例：ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceRendering ex:checklistMarkdown ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceRubric|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "guidance rubric"
msgstr "指导评量表"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceRubric|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A rubric the guidance set applies, reusing the norms rubric rather than minting a parallel assessment vocabulary. Multi-valued."
msgstr "该指导集所施用的一份评量表，复用规范切片的评量表，而非另铸一套平行的评估词汇。多值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceRubric|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceRubric ex:adrQualityRubric ."
msgstr "示例：ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceRubric ex:adrQualityRubric ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceVersionMembership|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "guidance version membership"
msgstr "指导之版本归属"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceVersionMembership|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The standpoint-scoped membership relator placing this guidance set in its version lineage. Reused rather than re-minted, so guidance versioning behaves exactly as every other versioned entity does."
msgstr "把该指导集置入其版本沿革之中的、按立场限定作用域的归属关系。此处复用而非重铸，故指导的版本化行为与其他任何受版本管理的实体完全一致。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceVersionMembership|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceVersionMembership ex:guidanceV2 ."
msgstr "示例：ex:reviewGuidance gmeow:guidanceVersionMembership ex:guidanceV2 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/preparationActivity|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "preparation activity"
msgstr "准备活动"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/preparationActivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The domain binding of the kernel's preparation seam onto the provenance activity spine: the concrete activity that carried out a preparation step. Specializes the kernel property rather than duplicating it, which is the direction every bridge in this slice runs."
msgstr "把内核的准备接缝绑定到出处活动骨架上的领域绑定：即实际执行某个准备步骤的那项具体活动。它特化内核属性而非复制之——本切片的每一道桥都朝这个方向架设。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/preparationActivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:stageFiles gmeow:preparationActivity ex:ocrRun ."
msgstr "示例：ex:stageFiles gmeow:preparationActivity ex:ocrRun ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewAccumulatedRecord|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "review accumulated record"
msgstr "复核之累积记录"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewAccumulatedRecord|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Content seven of eight: notes, decisions, artifacts, receipts and the comparison with prior occurrences. Range the accumulated-record view (stated in prose)."
msgstr "八项内容之七：备注、决定、产出物、回执，以及与既往各次 occurrence 的比对。值域为累积记录视图（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewAccumulatedRecord|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewAccumulatedRecord ex:decisionLog ."
msgstr "示例：ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewAccumulatedRecord ex:decisionLog ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewApprovalsAndPending|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "review approvals and pending inputs"
msgstr "复核之审批与待办输入"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewApprovalsAndPending|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Content five of eight: outstanding authorizations and awaited inputs. Range the approvals view (stated in prose)."
msgstr "八项内容之五：尚未了结的授权与所等待的输入。值域为审批视图（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewApprovalsAndPending|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewApprovalsAndPending ex:pendingApprovals ."
msgstr "示例：ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewApprovalsAndPending ex:pendingApprovals ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewCurrentEnactment|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "review current enactment"
msgstr "复核之当前实施"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewCurrentEnactment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Content three of eight: the occurrence in progress and, through it, the exact input generation it pinned."
msgstr "八项内容之三：正在进行的 occurrence，以及经由它所固定的那个确切输入世代。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewCurrentEnactment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewCurrentEnactment ex:weekThirteen ."
msgstr "示例：ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewCurrentEnactment ex:weekThirteen ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewEffectStatus|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "review effect status"
msgstr "复核之效应状态"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewEffectStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Content six of eight: effect, reconciliation and compensation status. Range the effect-status view (stated in prose). The content an operator needs most when something went wrong at the boundary."
msgstr "八项内容之六：效应、核实与补偿的状态。值域为效应状态视图（以散文陈述）。当边界处出了岔子时，操作者最需要的正是这一项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewEffectStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewEffectStatus ex:sagaStatus ."
msgstr "示例：ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewEffectStatus ex:sagaStatus ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewFrontier|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "review frontier"
msgstr "复核之前沿"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewFrontier|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Content four of eight: the derived frontier with its recommendations and blockers."
msgstr "八项内容之四：带有推荐与阻塞的导出前沿。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewFrontier|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewFrontier ex:week13Frontier ."
msgstr "示例：ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewFrontier ex:week13Frontier ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewGoalAndRecurrence|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "review goal and recurrence"
msgstr "复核之目标与周期"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewGoalAndRecurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Content one of eight: the continuing goal and the recurrence issuing occurrences. Range the goal-and-recurrence view (stated in prose)."
msgstr "八项内容之一：持续目标，以及发出各次 occurrence 的周期性。值域为「目标与周期」视图（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewGoalAndRecurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewGoalAndRecurrence ex:goalSummary ."
msgstr "示例：ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewGoalAndRecurrence ex:goalSummary ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewOfCluster|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "review of cluster"
msgstr "对簇之复核"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewOfCluster|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a review projection to the cluster it presents. Functional."
msgstr "把一份复核投影关联到它所呈现的那个簇。函数性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewOfCluster|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewOfCluster ex:adrReviewCluster ."
msgstr "示例：ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewOfCluster ex:adrReviewCluster ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewPrescriptionLineage|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "review prescription lineage"
msgstr "复核之规定沿革"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewPrescriptionLineage|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Content two of eight: the current prescription and how it was revised to get here. Range the lineage view (stated in prose)."
msgstr "八项内容之二：当前规定，以及它一路被修订至此的经过。值域为沿革视图（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewPrescriptionLineage|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewPrescriptionLineage ex:processLineage ."
msgstr "示例：ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewPrescriptionLineage ex:processLineage ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewReceipt|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "review receipt"
msgstr "复核回执"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewReceipt|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The projection receipt disclosing what this view preserved and what it dropped, reusing the shipped receipt vocabulary rather than minting a parallel one. Functional and MANDATORY: an operator view that collapses coexisting standpoints without saying so misrepresents disagreement as consensus."
msgstr "披露此视图保全了什么、又舍弃了什么的投影回执，复用已随包发布的回执词汇，而非另铸一套平行的。函数性且为必备：一个把并存诸立场悄然塌缩、却不加说明的操作者视图，是把分歧当作共识来呈现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewReceipt|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewReceipt ex:projectionReceipt ."
msgstr "示例：ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewReceipt ex:projectionReceipt ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewTimelineRepresentation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "review timeline representation"
msgstr "复核之时间线呈现"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewTimelineRepresentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Content eight of eight: an exact, accessible graph or timeline rendering. Range the timeline view (stated in prose); its textual surface grounds in the lang: rendering vocabulary."
msgstr "八项内容之八：一份精确且无障碍的图或时间线呈现。值域为时间线视图（以散文陈述）；其文本表层锚定于 lang: 的呈现词汇。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewTimelineRepresentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewTimelineRepresentation ex:timelineGraph ."
msgstr "示例：ex:week13Review gmeow:reviewTimelineRepresentation ex:timelineGraph ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
msgid "The domain binding of the general prescription/enactment/commitment kernel onto continuing work.\n\nThe kernel is domain-neutral by construction: it is declared standalone in the reasoning namespace and takes no axiom edge into the gmeow: namespace, which is what lets one algebra serve a workflow, a DAG, a repeatable guide, a curriculum, a control plan and an organizational guide without privileging any of them. This slice is where the durable-work reading acquires its gmeow:-typed edges, and every bridge runs domain-specializes-kernel rather than the reverse.\n\nIt deliberately mints no second recommendation model: the derived frontier reaches the preference apparatus through gmeow:CandidateSet and gmeow:ComparisonContext, inheriting ties, positive incomparability and the no-context-free-winner discipline rather than reproducing them. It mints no second authority gate, no second budget and no second frontier for the same reason.\n\nThe operator review projection is honest about being a projection. Collapsing standpoint-indexed frontier classifications into one readable surface is a real loss, and it is disclosed on a projection receipt with an explicit preservation judgment rather than hidden — a review that presents coexisting disagreement as consensus would be the most consequential overclaim this surface could make."
msgstr "把通用的「规定／实施／承诺」内核绑定到持续性工作之上的领域绑定。\n\n该内核在构造上即是领域中立的：它在推理命名空间中被声明为独立自足，且不向 gmeow: 命名空间引出任何公理边——正因如此，同一套代数才能同时服务于工作流、DAG、可重复指南、课程体系、控制方案与组织规程，而不偏袒其中任何一者。本切片正是「持久性工作」这一读法取得其 gmeow: 类型化边的所在，且每一道桥都由领域方向去特化内核，而非反其道而行。\n\n它刻意不铸造第二套推荐模型：导出的前沿经由 gmeow:CandidateSet 与 gmeow:ComparisonContext 抵达偏好装置，从而承继并列、正面的不可比性，以及「不得有脱离语境之赢家」这一纪律，而不是把它们重新实现一遍。出于同样的理由，它也不铸造第二道权限闸门、第二套预算、第二个前沿。\n\n操作者复核投影对自己「只是投影」这件事是诚实的。把按立场索引的诸前沿分类塌缩为单一可读界面，是一项真实的损失；该损失记在带有明确保全判断的投影回执上，而非被掩盖——一份把并存的分歧呈现为共识的复核，将是此界面所能作出的、后果最为深重的过度主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "GMEOW Work-Orchestration Module"
msgstr "GMEOW 工作编排模块"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/work-orchestration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The work-orchestration module — the domain binding of the prescription/enactment/commitment kernel onto continuing work: the gmeow:WorkCluster spine, versioned guidance, contribution attribution, the frontier's bindings into the preference apparatus, and the operator review projection with its disclosed preservation judgment."
msgstr "工作编排模块——把「规定／实施／承诺」内核绑定到持续性工作之上的领域绑定：gmeow:WorkCluster 骨架、经版本化的指导、贡献归属、前沿通往偏好装置的各项绑定，以及带有已披露保全判断的操作者复核投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Names the PROVENANCE of a contribution, not its quality or its correctness. A model contribution may be better reasoned than an operator one and still may not decide: the kind fixes what authority the contribution can carry, and advice is the ceiling for this kind regardless of how good the advice is."
msgstr "它标注贡献的来源，而非其质量或正确性。模型贡献可能比操作者贡献推理得更好，却仍然不能作出决定：种类决定了贡献可承载的权威，而对本种类而言，建议就是上限，无论建议本身多么出色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:c-114 gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionModel ; gmeow:clusterNote ex:cluster-migration ."
msgstr "示例：ex:c-114 gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionModel ; gmeow:clusterNote ex:cluster-migration 。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Records that a human authored the contribution; it does not by itself record WHICH human, nor that the human was entitled to decide. Attribution and entitlement are separate facts carried by the approval commitment, so this kind is a necessary and not a sufficient condition for a decision."
msgstr "它记录该贡献出自人类之手；但其本身既不记录出自哪一位人类，也不记录此人是否有权作出决定。归属与授权是由批准承诺所承载的另外两项事实，因此本种类只是决定的必要条件，而非充分条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:c-115 gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionOperator ; gmeow:approvalGoverningNorm ex:change-policy-v3 ."
msgstr "示例：ex:c-115 gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionOperator ; gmeow:approvalGoverningNorm ex:change-policy-v3 。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionTool|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Covers deterministic tools whose output is reproducible from their inputs — a linter, a digest, a query. It does not cover a sampling or otherwise non-reproducible tool: whatever cannot be re-derived is advice, not observation, and belongs under the model kind however mechanical its packaging."
msgstr "涵盖那些输出可由输入复现的确定性工具——代码检查器、摘要计算、查询。不涵盖抽样式或其他不可复现的工具：凡不能重新推导者，即属建议而非观察，无论其外壳多么机械，都应归入模型种类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionTool|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:c-116 gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionTool ; gmeow:explanationEvidence ex:digest-check-run-9 ."
msgstr "示例：ex:c-116 gmeow:contributionKind gmeow:contributionTool ; gmeow:explanationEvidence ex:digest-check-run-9 。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContributionKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Closed and mandatory, so there is no unclassified contribution and no room to add a fourth kind locally. The three values differ in authority rather than in quality, so a contribution is never promoted from one kind to another by being good."
msgstr "它是封闭且强制的，因此不存在未分类的贡献，也无从在本地添加第四个种类。三个取值的区别在于权威而非质量，所以一项贡献绝不会因为出色而由此种类升入彼种类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FrontierExplanation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Carries five required contents, and dissent is one of them rather than a courtesy. An explanation that omits the disagreeing observations manufactures a consensus, so completeness here is a correctness property and not a presentation preference."
msgstr "它承载五项必备内容，其中异议是必备之一，而非出于礼貌。若解释省略了持异见的观察，便是在制造共识，因此此处的完备性是正确性属性，而非呈现风格上的偏好。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GuidanceSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Versioned through the standard version-membership relator rather than a bespoke mechanism, because which guidance governed THAT occurrence must stay answerable after the guidance has moved on. An unversioned guidance set makes every past occurrence unauditable."
msgstr "它通过标准的版本归属关系体来版本化，而非另立机制，因为在指引本身演进之后，那一次occurrence究竟由哪一版指引所治理，必须仍然可以回答。未加版本的指引集会使所有过往occurrence无法审计。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/WorkCluster|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The thing that persists between occurrences, so it is never itself enacted. Enacting a cluster is a category error: occurrences are enacted, and the cluster is what makes them comparable to one another."
msgstr "它是在各次occurrence之间持存之物，因此其本身从不被执行。执行一个工作簇属于范畴错误：被执行的是occurrence，而工作簇是使这些occurrence彼此可比的东西。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/WorkReviewProjection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A projection, so it is lossy by construction and must disclose what it dropped through its receipt. A view that presents eight contents without a receipt is claiming completeness it cannot support."
msgstr "它是一种投影，按构造即有损，必须凭其回执披露自己舍弃了什么。若某视图罗列八项内容却不附回执，便是在主张一种它无从支撑的完备性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/approvalGoverningNorm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A domain specialization of the kernel seam, so it narrows the kernel property rather than competing with it. Using the kernel property directly in this slice would leave the policy an opaque reference instead of a real norm."
msgstr "它是内核接缝的领域特化，因而是收窄内核属性，而非与之竞争。若在本切片中直接使用内核属性，政策便只是一个不透明的引用，而非真正的规范。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterActivePrescription|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Deliberately a POINTER, not a record of what any occurrence ran. An enactment pins its version at start, so moving this pointer mid-flight revises what happens next without rewriting what is already running."
msgstr "它有意被设计为指针，而非任何一次occurrence实际运行内容的记录。执行在启动时便固定其版本，因此中途移动此指针只会改变此后发生之事，而不会改写正在运行之事。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterEnactment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Append-only history: a prior occurrence stays readable and comparable after later ones begin. Removing an occurrence to tidy the cluster destroys the comparison the cluster exists to support."
msgstr "这是只增不删的历史：后来的occurrence开始之后，先前的occurrence仍然可读、可比。为整洁而删去某次occurrence，恰恰摧毁了工作簇赖以存在的那种比较。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Where the goal is a maintenance goal, a successful occurrence never closes it: the goal holds only while its condition does, so the cluster keeps recurring by design rather than by oversight."
msgstr "若该目标属于维持型目标，则一次成功的occurrence绝不会将其关闭：目标只在其条件成立期间成立，因此工作簇的反复出现出于设计，而非出于疏忽。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterGuidanceSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A pointer like the active prescription, so an occurrence records the version it actually ran under rather than inheriting whatever this later points at. Reading guidance through this pointer retroactively rewrites history."
msgstr "它与活动处方一样是指针，因此occurrence记录的是自己实际据以运行的版本，而不承袭此指针日后所指之物。若透过此指针去读取指引，便会追溯性地改写历史。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterNote|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Retention between occurrences is the point: a cluster that forgets what the last occurrence learned is a schedule, not a continuing body of work. Notes are therefore cluster-scoped rather than occurrence-scoped."
msgstr "要害在于跨occurrence的留存：若某工作簇遗忘了上一次occurrence所学到的东西，那它便只是一份日程，而非持续的工作体。因此笔记的作用域是工作簇，而非单次occurrence。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterOccurrenceSeries|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Reused from the events spine, never re-minted: the recurrence rule belongs to the series, so a skipped occurrence is a schedule exception rather than a missing member of a list."
msgstr "它复用事件主干而绝不另铸：周期规则属于该序列，因此被跳过的occurrence是日程上的例外，而不是名单中缺失的一员。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Non-functional on purpose: several norms may govern one cluster, and where they disagree the disagreement is data rather than an error to resolve by picking one. Collapsing them would hide a real governance conflict."
msgstr "它有意不设为函数性：同一个工作簇可能受多条规范治理，而它们的分歧本身就是数据，并非靠择一而定即可消解的错误。若将其合并，就会掩盖真实存在的治理冲突。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/clusterSchedule|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The schedule is the GENERATOR: an enactment is generated by an occurrence rather than being one. Reading the schedule as the work itself is what makes an active recurrence over failing occurrences look healthy."
msgstr "日程是生成器：执行由occurrence所生成，而其本身并非occurrence。把日程当作工作本身来读，正是活跃的周期设定即便其下occurrence接连失败也仍显得一切正常的原因。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contributionKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Functional and mandatory, so a contribution without a kind is not merely under-annotated but unusable: the whole authority chain reads this value, and its absence leaves advice and decision indistinguishable."
msgstr "它既是函数性的也是强制的，因此没有种类的贡献不只是注记不足，而是根本无法使用：整条权威链条都要读取此值，缺了它，建议与决定便无从分辨。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/criterionMagnitude|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Grounds in the mathematical quantity spine so the magnitude travels with its dimension rather than as a bare number. A quantitative claim without a dimension cannot be compared across criteria, which is the only thing a criterion is for."
msgstr "它以数学量纲主干为根基，使数值随其量纲一同传递，而不是以裸数字出现。没有量纲的定量主张无法在不同准则之间比较，而比较恰恰是准则唯一的用处。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/enactmentContextAssembly|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Records what was WITHHELD as well as what was surfaced, so the answer to which notes this run saw is complete rather than one-sided. Functional: one assembly per occurrence, because two would make the answer ambiguous."
msgstr "它既记录被呈现之物，也记录被扣留之物，从而使这一次运行看到了哪些笔记这一问题得到完整而非片面的答复。它是函数性的：每次occurrence只有一份装配，若有两份，答案便含混不清。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/entryHardFailure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Reuses the preference slice's hard-constraint apparatus, which already guarantees that a hard failure may not be traded away by a favourable score elsewhere. Minting a local severity flag here would lose exactly that guarantee."
msgstr "它复用偏好切片的硬约束机制，该机制已经保证硬性失败不可用别处的高分来抵换。若在此另铸一个本地的严重程度标志，失去的恰恰是这项保证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explainsEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Functional, so an explanation accounts for exactly one entry. An explanation covering several entries would let the proof offered for one position be read as support for another."
msgstr "它是函数性的，因此一份解释恰好交代一个条目。若一份解释涵盖多个条目，为某一立场所提供的证明便可能被读作对另一立场的支持。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationCriterion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Reuses the norms criterion vocabulary rather than minting a local one, and its magnitudes ground in the mathematical quantity spine. Bare numbers here would be incomparable across entries, which defeats the point of ranking them."
msgstr "它复用规范切片的准则词汇，而不另铸本地词汇，其量值以数学量纲主干为根基。此处若用裸数字，各条目之间便无从比较，排序也就失去了意义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationDissent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Required wherever dissent exists, not offered as a courtesy. Suppressing an attributed disagreement turns coexisting standpoints into a manufactured consensus, which is the specific failure this content was added to prevent."
msgstr "凡有异议之处即为必备，而非出于礼貌的附赠。压下已具名的异议，会把并存的立场变成人为制造的共识，而这正是增设此项内容所要防止的具体失败。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationEvidence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Multi-valued and about the entry's position rather than about the enactment as a whole. Evidence for the run at large belongs on the run; putting it here would make every entry look equally supported."
msgstr "它是多值的，且针对该条目的立场，而非针对整次执行。关乎整次执行的证据应挂在执行之上；若放在此处，每个条目看起来都会同样有据可依。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Multi-valued because several norms may bear on one action and disagree; all are surfaced rather than reconciled. Choosing one here would present a governance judgment as if it were a fact about the entry."
msgstr "它是多值的，因为可能有多条规范同时作用于一个动作并彼此分歧；这些规范一律被呈现，而不加以调和。若在此择一，便是把治理判断当作关于该条目的事实来呈现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/explanationProof|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A model-generated narrative may never occupy this position. The slot is for a checkable derivation, and admitting prose here would let a plausible story stand where a verifiable argument is required."
msgstr "由模型生成的叙述绝不可占据此位置。此槽位专供可核验的推导，若在此接纳散文，便会让一段听来合理的说辞取代本该提供的可验证论证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/frontierCandidateSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The binding that gives the frontier ties, incomparability and transparent comparison for free, by routing through the existing preference apparatus instead of a second recommendation model. A local ranking here would be that forbidden second model."
msgstr "正是这一绑定，使前沿无偿获得并列、不可比与透明比较，因为它取道既有的偏好机制，而非另设一套推荐模型。若在此自行排序，那就是被禁止的第二套模型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/frontierComparisonContext|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Recommendations without a context are the context-free global winner the preference apparatus exists to forbid, so this binding is what keeps a ranking honest. Functional: two contexts would produce two rankings presented as one."
msgstr "没有语境的推荐，正是偏好机制所要禁止的那种脱离语境的全局赢家，因此这一绑定才是排序得以诚实的保障。它是函数性的：两个语境会产出两份排序，却被当作一份呈现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceChecklist|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Its content is an information object whose textual surface grounds in the linguistic form vocabulary, not a bare string on the guidance set. That indirection is what lets a checklist be rendered, translated and versioned like any other authored text."
msgstr "其内容是一个信息对象，其文本表层以语言形式词汇为根基，而不是挂在指引集上的裸字符串。正是这层间接，使清单能够像其他撰写文本一样被渲染、翻译与版本化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceRendering|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The seam through which this slice's prose content gets a linguistic form rather than floating as an untyped literal. It applies to any item carrying authored prose — guidance, notes, dissent, review renderings — and not only to guidance items."
msgstr "它是本切片的散文内容得以获得语言形式、而非以无类型字面量漂浮的接缝。它适用于任何承载撰写散文的项目——指引、笔记、异议、评审呈现——而不限于指引项目。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceRubric|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Reuses the norms rubric rather than minting a parallel assessment vocabulary, so a rubric applied here scores exactly as it does everywhere else. A local rubric would silently diverge as the shared one improves."
msgstr "它复用规范切片的评分量表，而不另铸一套并行的评估词汇，因此在此处套用的量表与别处评分完全一致。若自设本地量表，随着共享量表的改进，二者便会悄然分歧。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guidanceVersionMembership|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Reused rather than re-minted, so guidance versioning behaves exactly as every other versioned entity does. The membership is standpoint-scoped, which is what lets two standpoints disagree about which version was in force without one overwriting the other."
msgstr "它是复用而非另铸，因此指引的版本化行为与其他任何被版本化的实体完全一致。该归属受立场限定，正因如此，两种立场才能就当时生效的是哪一版本各执一词，而不至于彼此覆盖。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/preparationActivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The domain binding of the kernel's preparation seam onto the provenance activity spine, specializing the kernel property rather than duplicating it. That direction is the one every bridge in this slice runs, and reversing it would make the domain the authority."
msgstr "它把内核的准备接缝绑定到溯源活动主干之上，是对内核属性的特化而非复制。本切片中每一座桥梁都循此方向，若方向倒置，领域切片便反客为主成了权威。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewAccumulatedRecord|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Content seven of eight, and the only one that reaches backwards: it carries the comparison with prior occurrences. A review that drops it still shows the current run but loses the reason the cluster is a cluster."
msgstr "这是八项内容中的第七项，也是唯一回溯既往的一项：它承载与先前occurrence的比较。评审若舍去此项，仍能展示当前运行，却失去了工作簇之所以成其为工作簇的理由。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewApprovalsAndPending|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Content five of eight, covering outstanding authorizations and awaited inputs together because both are things the run is waiting on. Separating them would hide that an operator decision and an external arrival block work in the same way."
msgstr "这是八项内容中的第五项，把尚待授权与所待输入合并呈现，因为二者都是该次运行正在等待之物。若将它们拆开，就会掩盖操作者决定与外部到达以同样方式阻塞工作这一事实。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewCurrentEnactment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Content three of eight, and it reaches the exact input generation the occurrence pinned rather than the current one. Showing the live inputs instead would make a past run look as though it read data it never saw."
msgstr "这是八项内容中的第三项，且它触及的是该occurrence所固定的那一确切输入世代，而非当前世代。若改为展示实时输入，过去的运行看起来就像读取了它从未见过的数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewEffectStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Content six of eight, and the content an operator needs most when something went wrong at the boundary. It carries effect, reconciliation and compensation together because a boundary problem is never legible from any one of the three alone."
msgstr "这是八项内容中的第六项，也是边界处出岔子时操作者最需要的内容。它把效果、对账与补偿一并承载，因为边界问题绝无可能仅凭三者之一读懂。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewFrontier|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Content four of eight, presenting the DERIVED frontier with its recommendations and blockers. A review that presents a hand-curated action list in its place shows an opinion where the projection promises a derivation."
msgstr "这是八项内容中的第四项，呈现的是推导得出的前沿及其推荐与阻碍。评审若以人工挑选的行动清单取而代之，便是在投影承诺推导之处摆上了一份意见。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewGoalAndRecurrence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Content one of eight, pairing the continuing goal with the recurrence that issues occurrences. The pairing is deliberate: a goal shown without its recurrence invites the reader to expect a closing run that will never come."
msgstr "这是八项内容中的第一项，把持续性目标与签发occurrence的周期设定并列呈现。这一并列出于刻意：若只显示目标而不显示其周期，读者便会期待一次永远不会到来的收官运行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewOfCluster|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Functional, so one projection presents one cluster. A projection spanning several clusters would leave its receipt unable to say what it dropped from which, which is the disclosure the projection exists to make."
msgstr "它是函数性的，因此一份投影只呈现一个工作簇。若某份投影横跨多个工作簇，其回执便无从说明它从哪一个之中舍弃了什么，而这项披露正是投影存在的意义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewPrescriptionLineage|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Content two of eight: the current prescription AND how it was revised to get here. The lineage is what lets a reader judge whether a surprising instruction is new or long-standing, which the current version alone cannot say."
msgstr "这是八项内容中的第二项：当前处方，以及它如何一路修订至此。正是这条谱系，使读者能够判断某条出人意料的指示究竟是新近添加还是由来已久，而仅凭当前版本无从知晓。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewReceipt|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Functional and MANDATORY, because an operator view that collapses coexisting standpoints without saying so misrepresents disagreement as agreement. The receipt is what makes the projection's losses visible rather than silent."
msgstr "它既是函数性的，也是强制的，因为若操作者视图把并存的立场悄然压平，就会把分歧误现为一致。回执使投影的损失显露在外，而非无声无息。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/reviewTimelineRepresentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Content eight of eight, and required to be exact as well as accessible: a rendering that simplifies the graph for legibility is a different projection with its own losses, which its own receipt would have to disclose."
msgstr "这是八项内容中的第八项，既要求可访问，也要求精确：若某种呈现为了易读而简化了图，那它就是另一种投影，带有自己的损失，须由其自身的回执加以披露。"
